From 573c731d6056dd29d06ae7c86eacb220d685d292 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sergey Strebulaev <s@vivantel.dev>
Date: Sun, 30 Aug 2026 01:46:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 07/15] feat: role lists, decision scope/expires,
 no-audit-log-facts, lint, query
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

steward and bootstrap now enforce every rule this session's roadmap
interview produced, in the same pass that added the guardrails
describing them — not deferred to a plan. A guardrail in
docs/guardrails/ never ships to anyone who installs the plugin; only a
skill's own body does, so deferring the enforcement would have meant
kms's actual users got nothing from this work. steward gained a
principle stating this directly, plus three new checks (decision past
expires, fact reads like a log, role list stale) so the same mistake
gets caught even if it recurs.

bootstrap now compiles two role lists (product-track-roles.md,
process-track-roles.md) as an extension of its existing
skill-gap-detection scan — AI-agent review perspectives per track, not
human staffing, consulted by roadmap while drafting a decision of that
track when they exist. Decisions may carry optional scope/expires
fields for work that's bounded or provisional (a hypothesis test, a
temporary workaround) instead of being treated as permanent once
accepted. Facts that read as ungrounded, unreferenced event logs are
now explicitly out of bounds — kms is a knowledge base, not a
dashboard or log.

Two new skills close a gap in the existing six: lint runs steward's
kind of structural checks as a full-repo, on-demand sweep instead of a
session-diff (steward can't catch rot predating whatever session
happens to run it), and query answers a question from the knowledge
base with citations instead of leaving that to manual grep — every
other skill in this plugin writes to the knowledge base, none of them
had answered a question from it.

Refs: docs/decisions/0013-ai-agent-role-lists-per-track.md
